###    - Execution times for performance analysis
###    - Retry attempt counts and strategies
###    - Service health scores and error rates
###
### 4. REAL-TIME UPDATES:
###    - Events published to pub/sub for live dashboard updates
###    - WebSocket integration for instant notifications
###    - Live status updates in React notifications UI
###
### 5. CIRCUIT BREAKER MONITORING:
###    - Live status of service health and failure counts
###    - State transitions (closed → open → half-open)
###    - Failure threshold monitoring and alerts
###
### 6. RETRY PATTERN VISUALIZATION:
###    - Exponential backoff progression demonstration
###    - Fixed interval vs linear backoff comparison
###    - Success/failure rates across retry strategies
###
### 7. CASCADE FAILURE ANALYSIS:
###    - Track how failures propagate through services
###    - Dependency mapping and impact assessment
###    - Containment effectiveness measurement
###
### 8. RECOVERY MONITORING:
###    - System recovery time measurements
###    - Circuit breaker reset detection
###    - Service health restoration tracking
###
### 9. PERFORMANCE METRICS:
###    - Response time degradation during failures
###    - Throughput impact measurement
###    - Resource utilization under stress
###
### 10. HEALTH MONITORING:
###     - Before/after system health comparisons
###     - Service availability percentages
###     - Multi-dimensional health scoring
###
### =============================================
### 🚀 DEMO EXECUTION GUIDE:
###
### TIMING: Execute scenarios in phases with 30-60 second delays
### MONITORING: Keep notifications UI (localhost:8080) open during demo
### OBSERVATION: Watch circuit-breakers endpoint for state changes
### ANALYSIS: Use correlation IDs to trace complete workflows
### CLEANUP: Scenarios automatically expire based on duration_seconds
###
### EXPECTED DEMO DURATION: 10-15 minutes for complete demonstration
### CONCURRENT SCENARIOS: Up to 4 scenarios can run simultaneously
### NOTIFICATION RATE: Expect 20-50 events per minute during active chaos
### =============================================


### =============================================
### CIRCUIT BREAKER DEMONSTRATION GUIDE
### =============================================
### To properly demonstrate circuit breaker functionality:
###
### 1. BASELINE: Run GET /circuit-breakers (should show all closed)
### 2. START CHAOS: Execute scenarios from chaos-demo.http
### 3. STRESS TEST: Submit orders above while chaos is active
### 4. MONITOR: Watch circuit-breakers endpoint for state changes
### 5. OBSERVE: Note how circuit breakers protect against cascade failures
###
### Circuit Breaker States:
### - CLOSED: Normal operation, requests pass through
### - OPEN: Too many failures, requests fail fast (no retry)
### - HALF-OPEN: Testing if service has recovered
###
### Expected Behavior During Chaos:
### - Failure count increases as services fail
### - State transitions from closed → open after threshold
### - Fast failures protect system from cascade effects
### =============================================
